  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "Which of the following is equal to\n\n\\[1 + \\cfrac{1}{1 + \\cfrac{1}{1 + 1}}?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{4}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{3}{2}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{3}\\)",
    "D": "\\(2\\)",
    "E": "\\(3\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Evaluate the innermost denominator first: \\(1+1=2\\). The denominator of the outer fraction is then\n\\[\n1+\\frac12=\\frac32.\n\\]\nThe reciprocal of this positive number is \\(\\frac23\\), so the full expression equals\n\\[\n1+\\frac{1}{3/2}=1+\\frac23=\\frac53.\n\\]\nBoth denominators are nonzero. The answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac53}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
